Last close: {{quote}}
Minute bars (last 30m): {{path}}
Recent tape (last 3m): {{tape}}
Other majors: {{others}}
State summary: {{summary.summary}}

Key drivers of 1-minute moves:
- Funding resets (minutes_to_funding near 0): can cause 5-15 bp moves as positions adjust
- Hour effects: US cash open (13:30-14:30 UTC) and Asia open (0:00-2:00 UTC) show elevated volatility
- Momentum continuation: strong taker_buy_share (>0.7 or <0.3) in recent bars often continues 1-2 minutes
- Cross-asset leadership: BTC often leads ETH/SOL by 1 minute; check if others moved first
- Volume surges: high volume bars (>2x average) with directional flow predict follow-through

Most 1-minute moves are under 2 bps. Predict larger moves only when:
- Near funding reset (<15 min) with directional tape
- Clear momentum in last 2-3 bars (same direction, strong taker imbalance)
- High volume breakout from recent range
- Cross-asset confirmation (BTC already moved, forecasting ETH/SOL)

For half_width: account for typical noise. Quiet hours need 2-3 bps width minimum. Active periods or post-move consolidation need 3-5 bps to avoid getting run over on noise.
